{
  "id": "ep216",
  "duration": 45.407,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.229,
      "text": "You do not need 25,000 miles per hour to escape Earth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The Blue Marble 4463x4163.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA. Photo taken by either Harrison Schmitt or Ron Evans (of the Apollo 17 crew).",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Blue_Marble_4463x4163.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 1.967,
          "end": 4.233,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.229,
      "end": 9.699,
      "text": "That massive speed is only required if you use a single unpowered launch boost.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "SaturnV S-IVB.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SaturnV_S-IVB.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.233,
          "end": 7.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 7.8,
          "end": 9.7,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9.699,
      "end": 17.144,
      "text": "If you fire a projectile and let gravity do all the work, you genuinely need 11.2 kilometers per second.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Apollo 11 Launch - GPN-2000-000630.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apollo_11_Launch_-_GPN-2000-000630.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 9.7,
          "end": 17.133,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.144,
      "end": 22.489,
      "text": "But modern rockets are not unpowered cannonballs designed for a single blast.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Space Shuttle Columbia launching.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Space_Shuttle_Columbia_launching.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.133,
          "end": 19.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 19.533,
          "end": 22.5,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 22.489,
      "end": 29.009,
      "text": "By keeping their engines burning, they can climb at a leisurely walking pace and still slip away completely.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "ISS031-E-103470 - View of Earth.jpg",
        "credit": "Earth Science and Remote Sensing Unit, Lyndon B. Johnson Space Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISS031-E-103470_-_View_of_Earth.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 22.5,
          "end": 25.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 25.967,
          "end": 29.0,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 29.009,
      "end": 34.759,
      "text": "Escape velocity is simply the total energy cost needed to leave Earth for good.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "ISS031-E-103470 - View of Earth.jpg",
        "credit": "Earth Science and Remote Sensing Unit, Lyndon B. Johnson Space Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISS031-E-103470_-_View_of_Earth.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 29.0,
          "end": 34.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 34.759,
      "end": 40.054,
      "text": "Thanks to continuous thrust, you do not have to pay that steep gravity bill all at once.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Voyager spacecraft.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Voyager_spacecraft.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 34.767,
          "end": 38.2,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 38.2,
          "end": 40.067,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 40.054,
      "end": 45.057,
      "text": "This is why you do not need 25,000 miles per hour to escape Earth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The Blue Marble 4463x4163.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA. Photo taken by either Harrison Schmitt or Ron Evans (of the Apollo 17 crew).",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Blue_Marble_4463x4163.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 40.067,
          "end": 45.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
